<p>Tucson runs on a different clock than most cities. Winter is the high season, the University of Arizona sets the rhythm from August to May, and every January and February the city turns into one of the world's biggest gem and mineral marketplace. If you time your effort to those cycles, the best side hustles in Tucson can pay surprisingly well, especially with living costs well below Phoenix.</p>
<p>This guide covers 17 side gigs that work here, what they typically pay, what they cost to start, and the local details that help you win clients, from Sam Hughes to Oro Valley.</p>

