<h2 id="start-in-tucson">How to start a side hustle in Tucson this month</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Match the gig to the season.</strong> Fall is the time to line up winter rental cleaning and gem show contacts; spring is when to sell home-watch routes.</li>
  <li><strong>Pick one lead source.</strong> Nextdoor and neighborhood Facebook groups for home services, campus boards for tutoring, apps for driving.</li>
  <li><strong>Price for profit.</strong> If you freelance, the <a href="/tools/freelance-rate-calculator/">freelance rate calculator</a> shows what you need to charge after fees and taxes.</li>
  <li><strong>Land three clients and collect reviews.</strong> Tucson is a word-of-mouth town; retirees refer friends.</li>
  <li><strong>Register if you sell goods.</strong> Get your TPT license before the gem show or market season.</li>
  <li><strong>Track everything.</strong> Use a separate bank account and log mileage from your first trip.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="arizona-tax-rules">Arizona taxes and rules for Tucson side income</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>State income tax:</strong> a flat 2.5% on taxable income.</li>
  <li><strong>Self-employment tax:</strong> 15.3% federal on net profit, plus federal income tax. The <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a> helps you estimate quarterly payments.</li>
  <li><strong>TPT license:</strong> Arizona taxes the seller through transaction privilege tax. If you sell goods at markets, online to Arizona buyers, or at the gem show, or you rent short-term, you need a TPT license from the Arizona Department of Revenue, which also administers the City of Tucson portion. Most personal services, like tutoring or pet sitting, are not subject to TPT.</li>
  <li><strong>Contractor limits:</strong> handyman jobs must stay under $1,000 total, with no permit required, to avoid needing a contractor license.</li>
  <li><strong>Food and rentals:</strong> food vending needs Pima County health permits. For short-term rentals, check whether Tucson or Pima County requires a local registration on top of your TPT license.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout"><strong>Quick tip:</strong> Gem show cash adds up quickly and is still taxable. Log every payment the day you get it so you are not reconstructing February in April.</div>

